t assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: relatively weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. So reliability, stress resilience good, but interpersonal issues (nasty remarks) affect crew cooperation, also memory for numbers could affect attention.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. So decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence good, but communication and teamwork issues, and lack of development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper. So reliability, problem solving, responsibility, but hot temper and know-it-all may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to weigh overall. Which candidate has strongest overall fit? All have some concerns. Candidate B has stress resilience and conscientiousness, but nasty remarks serious for crew cooperation. Candidate C has good decision making and calm, but egocentric and communication issues. Candidate D has responsibility and concentration, but hot temper. Candidate A has leadership but show-off and not open to new ideas.\n\nWhich is best? Perhaps Candidate D: strong responsibility, concentration, problem solving, adequate response to unexpected events. Hot temper is concerning but maybe manageable? Candidate B's nasty remarks may be more severe for crew environment. Candidate C's egocentric and communication issues also severe. Candidate A's show-off and not open to new ideas could affect adaptability.\n\nThus I might recommend Candidate D, but note concerns.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: none yet, but we can say \"Given the initial overview, I propose...\"\n\nWe must include explicit facts: D concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, responds to unexpected events adequately. Concern: hot temper, know-it-all.\n\nExplain why overall fit: strong reliability, technical competence, decision quality, responsibility, but temper is a concern but perhaps less than others' communication issues.\n\nThus vote for D.\n\nNow produce output."}
